title: Garlic Fried Rice Bowl
method: stovetop
source: https://www.americastestkitchen.com/recipes/14789-garlic-fried-rice
protein: none
ingredient_count: 4
---

  Transfer @jasmine rice{4½%cups}(cooked, cold) to #fine-mesh strainer{}. Place rice under cold running water and break up clumps with your hands. Let drain for ~{5%minutes}.

Combine @vegetable oil{3%tablespoons} and @garlic cloves{8}(chopped fine) in #12-inch nonstick skillet{}. Cook over medium heat until garlic turns golden brown, ~{3-5%minutes}.

Add rice and @kosher salt{1%teaspoon} and cook, stirring frequently, until garlic is evenly distributed throughout rice, about ~{2%minutes}.

Off heat, season with salt to taste. Transfer to #dish{}, sprinkle with @scallion{1}(sliced thin), and serve.